The complete 12165-byte proposal at SHA256 7b3be653187f3695934cd68d28812aa36e9e527d5cd33afad37df63a42fa501b was read before authoring the check. Direct control-block calculation supports the four-letter controlled X formula for both polarities. S X S*=Y supplies the six-letter Y factor, hence an XYX word costs 14 with no dropped phase. The commutator construction cancels on every failed control pattern. The parity induction gives T(k)<=(9k^2-c_k)/8, c_k=1 for odd k and 4 for even k.

The pivot-CNOT permutation maps any selected pair to one differing bit without phases; the controlled gate therefore has identity complement. Givens elimination must still apply its r>0 phase-fixing matrix when the lower entry is zero. The determinant projector expansion includes its empty-subset scalar. Logical routing uses CNOT words and never grants unequal-gap physical SWAP. The finite grid proof has a strict Frobenius margin after its extra sqrt(d) refinement, so it does not need exact zero or angle-branch decisions.

No load-bearing algebraic defect has been found analytically. The physical consequence will be stated conditionally on the corrected comb premises. Program, branch compilation, preparation, Hamiltonian and timing allowances must be separate. A final phase-generator allowance of order epsilon^5 and input arithmetic requests of order epsilon^9 are distinct; the proposal's phrase cancellation-amplitude tolerance needs that interpretation or a statement that it is a deliberately stronger tolerance. Nominal laboratory resources do not include classical oracle/compiler walltime.

